
These are versions of OHDSI sourced scripts to build tables for CDM and 
to load vocab files.

These versions split out into separate databases
* the vocab part
* the non vocab part (the "clinical data" part; which sometimes seems to be referred to as the cdm evn though only part of whole cdm) 
so that the same vocab part can be used with multiple non-vocab parts

Before splitting into two databases these files are (I believe) taken from 
https://github.com/OHDSI/CommonDataModel/tree/main/inst/ddl/5.4/sql_server
can't remember where got the vocab_load.sql from - there are various hints that this
is no longer so obviously centrally distribued for some reason to do with which team 
is responsible for it
(https://github.com/OHDSI/CommonDataModel/issues/487)

The sql scripts are parameterised so that db and schemas can be chosen

The two python scripts run the sql scripts

The parameterisation uses the syntax that sqlserver so could also use with small mods could used within SSMS using :setvar syntax (I think)
